{
  "moduleId": "m00336",
  "title": {
    "segmentId": "m00336:title:auto-1",
    "text": "The Citric Acid Cycle"
  },
  "documentClass": null,
  "metadata": {
    "uuid": "c66b6753-1830-4b45-b225-20a4c8d97ed3"
  },
  "content": [
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00001",
      "segmentId": "m00336:para:para-00001"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00002",
      "segmentId": "m00336:para:para-00002"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00001",
      "class": "mechanism-figure scaled-down",
      "caption": {
        "segmentId": "m00336:caption:fig-00001-caption"
      },
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00336:alt:fig-00001-alt",
          "text": "The eight-step citric acid  reaction cycle to convert acetyl CoA to two molecules of carbon dioxide and the  reduced coenzymes nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide phosphate hydride and flavin adenine dinucleotide dihydride."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_29_07_001.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "section",
      "id": "sect-00001",
      "class": null,
      "title": {
        "segmentId": "m00336:title:sect-00001-title",
        "text": "Step 1 of [[xref:fig-00001]]: Addition to Oxaloacetate"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "section",
          "id": "sect-00002",
          "class": null,
          "title": null,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00003",
              "segmentId": "m00336:para:para-00003"
            },
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00004",
              "segmentId": "m00336:para:para-00004"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00002",
              "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00336:alt:fig-00002-alt",
                  "text": "Acetyl coenzyme A condensation with oxaloacetate leads to (S)-Citryl coenzyme A, which is hydrolyzed to yield citrate and H S C o A."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_29_07_002.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "section",
          "id": "sect-00003",
          "class": null,
          "title": {
            "segmentId": "m00336:title:sect-00003-title",
            "text": "Step 2 of [[xref:fig-00001]]: Isomerization"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00005",
              "segmentId": "m00336:para:para-00005"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00003",
              "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00336:alt:fig-00003-alt",
                  "text": "Citrate with labeled pro-R and pro-S hydrogens undergoes dehydration to form cis-aconitate, which is further dehydrated to (2 R,3 S)-isocitrate."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_29_07_003.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "section",
          "id": "sect-00004",
          "class": null,
          "title": {
            "segmentId": "m00336:title:sect-00004-title",
            "text": "Step 3 of [[xref:fig-00001]]: Oxidation and Decarboxylation"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00006",
              "segmentId": "m00336:para:para-00006"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00004",
              "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00336:alt:fig-00004-alt",
                  "text": "(2 R,3 S)-isocitrate is oxidized by nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide cation to oxalosuccinate, followed by magnesium catalyzed decarboxylation, and protonation to  form  alpha-ketoglutarate."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_29_07_004.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "section",
          "id": "sect-00005",
          "class": null,
          "title": {
            "segmentId": "m00336:title:sect-00005-title",
            "text": "Step 4 of [[xref:fig-00001]]: Oxidative Decarboxylation"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00007",
              "segmentId": "m00336:para:para-00007"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00005",
              "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00336:alt:fig-00005-alt",
                  "text": "Alpha-ketoglutarate is converted to succinyl CoA via HS-CoA condensation, and nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide cation  mediated decarboxylation."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_29_07_005.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "section",
          "id": "sect-00006",
          "class": null,
          "title": {
            "segmentId": "m00336:title:sect-00006-title",
            "text": "Step 5 of [[xref:fig-00001]]: Acyl CoA Cleavage"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00008",
              "segmentId": "m00336:para:para-00008"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00006",
              "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00336:alt:fig-00006-alt",
                  "text": "Succinyl coenzyme A condenses with hydrogen phosphate to form an acyl phosphate which decomposes via an enzyme bond imidazole to succinate and guanosine triphosphate."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_29_07_006.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "section",
          "id": "sect-00007",
          "class": null,
          "title": {
            "segmentId": "m00336:title:sect-00007-title",
            "text": "Step 6 of [[xref:fig-00001]]: Dehydrogenation"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00009",
              "segmentId": "m00336:para:para-00009"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00007",
              "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00336:alt:fig-00007-alt",
                  "text": "Succinate is reduced by an enzyme-bonded flavin adenine dinucleotide to fumarate."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_29_07_007.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "section",
          "id": "sect-00008",
          "class": null,
          "title": {
            "segmentId": "m00336:title:sect-00008-title",
            "text": "Steps 7–8 of [[xref:fig-00001]]: Hydration and Oxidation"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00010",
              "segmentId": "m00336:para:para-00010"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00008",
              "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00336:alt:fig-00008-alt",
                  "text": "A base with a set of lone pair reacts with fumarate and water followed by stereoselective enolate protonation  to form (S)-Malate. "
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_29_07_008.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00011",
              "segmentId": "m00336:para:para-00011"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00009",
              "class": "unnumbered",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00336:alt:fig-00009-alt",
                  "text": "Acetyl-coenzyme A is oxidized via  nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide cation , flavin adenine dinucleotide, and guanine diphosphate to form two moles of carbon dioxide and H S C o A."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_29_07_009.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
